IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- THE NOUNS.
-- Plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-04-06; not the official text.
--
-- Nouns only: the people, facts and choices a witness of ordinary competence could
-- testify to, grouped by the Part of the Regulations that first needs them. Every
-- other spr-*.l4 module imports this one. Rules live in the Part modules.
-- The one function here is the YMD shim: YMD is missing from the stable prelude, so it
-- is defined once, here, and every importer gets it (a second definition anywhere would
-- make the name unusable in a module that imports both).

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YearMonthDay y m d MEANS Date d m y -- renamed from YMD so it cannot collide with the YMD in newer daydate libraries; see docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5

§ `Part 1 -- General`

-- Regulation 1(3): the Regulations (except Part 5) do not apply to a person who reaches
-- pensionable age before 6 April 2016. The text names that outcome, so it is a member of the result.
DECLARE `Whether the Regulations apply to a person` IS ONE OF
    `these Regulations apply to the person`
    `these Regulations do not apply to the person, who reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016`

-- Regulation 1(5): how two people are joined, and whether either of them is married to a third person.
DECLARE `How two people are joined` IS ONE OF
    `not married to each other and not civil partners`
    `married to each other`
    `civil partners of each other`

DECLARE `Two people at a time` HAS
    `how they are joined` IS A `How two people are joined`
    `either of them is married to a third person` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Regulation 1(4): "deferral period" means the period during which a person's entitlement to a state pension
-- under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred.
DECLARE `Deferral period` HAS
    `first day` IS A DATE
    `last day` IS A DATE

§ `Part 2 -- Prisoners`

-- Regulation 2(2): the kinds of custody that make a person "a prisoner" for regulation 2(1).
DECLARE `Kind of custody` IS ONE OF
    `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings`
    `unlawfully at large`
    `detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983`
    `detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`
    `in none of those kinds of custody`

-- Regulation 3(2): the sentences that, once imposed, take a remand outside regulation 3(1).
DECLARE `Kind of sentence` IS ONE OF
    `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings`
    `a sentence of detention where the provisions mentioned in regulation 2(2)(c)(i) or (d) apply`
    `a suspended sentence within the meaning in section 286 of the Sentencing Code`
    `a sentence of none of those kinds`

DECLARE `Sentence imposed` HAS
    `its kind` IS A `Kind of sentence`
    `it was imposed outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- One day of a person's custody. The same record carries the remand facts, because regulation 3 modifies
-- regulation 2(1) for the same days.
DECLARE `A day of a person's custody` HAS
    `the day` IS A DATE
    `the kind of custody` IS A `Kind of custody`
    `in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- The release date the Secretary of State has certified under section 50(3) of the Mental Health Act 1983, if any.
    `the release date the Secretary of State has certified` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `remanded in custody for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sentence later imposed for that offence` IS A MAYBE `Sentence imposed`

§ `Part 3 -- Deferral of State Pension`

-- Regulations 5(2), 7(2): how a choice, an application or a notice is given.
DECLARE `Manner of giving` IS ONE OF
    `in writing`
    `by telephone`
    `in some other way`

DECLARE `How something was given` HAS
    `the manner` IS A `Manner of giving`
    `the office or telephone number used was specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State directed in the case that the written manner must be used` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Sections 8 and 9 of the 2014 Act (and, in Part 6, regulations 19 and 20): the two things a person may choose to be paid.
DECLARE `Payment chosen` IS ONE OF
    `a lump sum`
    `a state pension`

-- Regulation 4: where a choice falls against the period for making it.
DECLARE `Where a choice falls against its period` IS ONE OF
    `within the period for making the choice`
    `after the period, so that it can only be a late choice`
    `before the period begins, which the text does not provide for`

DECLARE `Facts for the period for a choice` HAS
    -- The dates in the notices, issued before the choice was made, that confirm the person may make the choice.
    `dates in the notices confirming that the person may make the choice` IS A LIST OF DATE
    `the date the person claimed a state pension` IS A DATE
    `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE
    `the date the choice was made` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Facts for a late choice` HAS
    `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
    `any amount was paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Regulation 6(2): the circumstances in which a choice may be altered.
DECLARE `Application to alter a choice` HAS
    `the person who made the choice has not subsequently died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an application is made to alter the choice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date in the notification confirming the choice that has been made` IS A DATE
    `the date the application is made` IS A DATE
    `the application is made within a longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how the application is made` IS A `How something was given`
    `the choice that has been made` IS A `Payment chosen`
    `the choice the application would substitute` IS A `Payment chosen`
    `any amount was paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has been repaid in full` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was repaid within the period in paragraph (2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount paid by way of a state pension` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum` IS A NUMBER
    `an alteration has already been made in respect of the same deferral` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Social Security (Claims and Payments) Regulations 1987` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Regulation 7: suspending entitlement.
DECLARE `Notice suspending entitlement` HAS
    `the person has become entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has given notice to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how the notice was given` IS A `How something was given`

-- Regulation 8: the date from which a suspension takes effect.
DECLARE `Facts for the start of a suspension` HAS
    `the date on which the option was exercised` IS A DATE
    `the date the person specifies` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- Regulation 9: cancelling a suspension.
DECLARE `Facts for cancelling a suspension` HAS
    `the person opted to suspend entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person made a claim for a state pension whilst it was suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date on which the person cancels the suspension` IS A DATE
    `the first day of the past period` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the past period` IS A DATE

-- Regulation 11(2)(a): the benefits that stop a day counting. One day can fall under one or several; the
-- facts for a day name the one the person received (or none).
DECLARE `Benefit that stops a day counting` IS ONE OF
    `state pension credit`
    `income support`
    `an income-related employment and support allowance`
    `an income-based jobseeker's allowance`
    `universal credit`
    `a carer's allowance`
    `the carer support payment component of carer support`
    `an unemployability supplement`
    `severe disablement allowance`
    `a widow's pension`
    `a widowed mother's allowance`
    `incapacity benefit`
    `none of those benefits`

DECLARE `A day of the deferral period` HAS
    `the benefit the person received on the day` IS A `Benefit that stops a day counting`
    -- Regulation 11(2)(b): someone received an increase of one of those benefits in respect of the person.
    `an increase of one of those benefits was received in respect of the person on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person who received the increase and the person whose entitlement is deferred` IS A `Two people at a time`
    `they reside together` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Regulation 11(2)(c): the custody facts of the day, read by regulations 2 and 3.
    `the person's custody on the day` IS A `A day of a person's custody`

-- Regulation 12A: a stretch of the deferral period between two non-uprating changes.
DECLARE `Modification period` HAS
    `first day` IS A DATE
    `last day` IS A DATE

§ `Part 5 -- Amendments to other legislation (the Schedule: sharing of state pension rights)`

-- The Schedule inserts regulation 6 into the Sharing of State Scheme Rights (Provision of Information and Valuation)
-- (No.2) Regulations 2000. Paragraph (1) says what the Secretary of State must furnish; these are the things furnished.
DECLARE `Item of information about sharing` IS ONE OF
    `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the date the request is received`
    `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the relevant date`
    `a valuation of the previous shareable old state scheme rights as at the relevant date`
    `the amount of the former entitlement to a category A retirement pension by virtue of section 44(3)(b) of the 1992 Act, as at the relevant date and immediately before 6 April 2016`
    `an explanation of the shareable new state scheme rights, of the effect of a pension sharing order or provision, of how the spouse or civil partner becomes entitled, and of how that differs from shared additional pension`

DECLARE `Request for information about sharing` HAS
    `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or the order` IS A DATE
    -- The relevant date has the meaning given by section 10(3) of the Family Law (Scotland) Act 1985; there is none in
    -- proceedings to which that Act does not apply.
    `the relevant date` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the request or order includes a valuation under paragraphs (2), (3) or (4) or an amount under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person notified the Secretary of State by then that the information is needed in connection with proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day of a shorter period specified by the court in an order` IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Part 6 -- Graduated Retirement Benefit`

-- A surviving spouse or civil partner, and the person who died. Dates are data: the question is asked as at a date,
-- and "under" and "over" pensionable age are comparisons of dates.
DECLARE `Facts about a survivor` HAS
    `the date as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
    `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS A DATE
    `the date the deceased died` IS A DATE
    -- NOTHING where the deceased died before reaching pensionable age.
    `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE
    `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Paragraph of regulation 16 a survivor falls within` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 16(1)`
    `regulation 16(2)`
    `regulation 16(3)`
    `none of regulation 16(1), (2) or (3)`

DECLARE `Facts for the up-rating of a survivor's state pension` HAS
    -- Regulation 17(2): the rate without any reduction under regulations made under section 7(4) of the 2014 Act, taking into
    -- account any reduction under section 14 of that Act, and without any increase under section 17 of that Act.
    `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15` IS A NUMBER
    `the sum of the rates of any state pension the person is entitled to under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act` IS A NUMBER
    `the full rate of the state pension immediately before any increase` IS A NUMBER
    `the full rate of the state pension after an increase, if the full rate is increased` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    -- A percentage as a fraction: 4% is entered as 4%.
    `the percentage specified in an uprating order, if one comes into force` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

DECLARE `Which up-rating case of regulation 17 applies` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 17(3) and (4): the pension rises by the same percentage as the full rate`
    `regulation 17(5) to (7): the pension rises by a percentage of the shortfall, the excess, or both`
    `regulation 17(8) and (9): the pension rises by the percentage in the uprating order`

DECLARE `A choice made under regulation 18` HAS
    `the payment chosen` IS A `Payment chosen`
    `how the choice was made` IS A `How something was given`
    `the facts for the period` IS A `Facts for the period for a choice`
    `the facts for a late choice` IS A `Facts for a late choice`

DECLARE `Facts for the payment under regulation 18` HAS
    `the choice the person made, if any` IS A MAYBE `A choice made under regulation 18`
    `the period for making a choice has ended without one being made` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `What is paid under regulation 18` IS ONE OF
    `a lump sum under regulation 19`
    `a state pension under regulation 20`
    `nothing yet, because the person can still make a choice`
    `the Regulations do not say, because the choice was made before its period began`

§ `Part 7 -- Overseas Residents`

-- "Overseas resident" is not defined in these Regulations (it is the 2014 Act's), so it is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `When an up-rating increase falls against the deferral period` IS ONE OF
    `in respect of the deferral period`
    `after the deferral period ended`
    `at some other time`

DECLARE `Facts about an up-rating increase for a person abroad` HAS
    `Regulations have been made providing that regulation 21 applies to the up-rating increase` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's entitlement to a state pension had been deferred for a period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `when the deferral period ended the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `when the deferral period ended the person was an overseas resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `where the increase falls against the deferral period` IS A `When an up-rating increase falls against the deferral period`
    `the person was an overseas resident at the time of the increase` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person continued to be an overseas resident until the deferral period ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act immediately before the increase` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `What regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 21 takes the increase away from the person`
    `regulation 21 does not take the increase away from the person`
    `regulation 21 does not apply to this increase, because no Regulations have been made applying it`

DECLARE `A part of the deferral period, abroad or not` HAS
    `the first day of the part` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the part` IS A DATE
    `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Which weekly rate an increment is a percentage of` IS ONE OF
    `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part`
    `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part`
    `the Regulations do not say, because the person was an overseas resident who was in Great Britain or a specified territory`

§ `Part 8 -- National Insurance Credits`

-- A week is identified by its first day. Regulation 25(3) puts a week that straddles two tax years in the one it begins in.
-- Lower earnings limits, qualifying earnings factors and the other figures of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992
-- and the 1975 Regulations are not among the inputs: they are stated inputs wherever a rule needs one.

DECLARE `Whether a credit is given` IS ONE OF
    `the credit is given`
    `the credit is not given`
    `the credit is left to the Secretary of State's discretion`

-- Regulation 29(2): the provisions of the 1975 Regulations whose credits also count for the 2014 Act.
DECLARE `Provision of the 1975 Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 7 (credits for approved training)`
    `regulation 7A (credits for carer's allowance or carer support payment)`
    `regulation 7B (credits for disability element of working tax credit)`
    `regulation 8A (credits for unemployment)`
    `regulation 8B (credits for incapacity for work or limited capability for work)`
    `regulation 9B (credits for jury service)`
    `regulation 9C (credits for maternity pay etc.)`
    `regulation 9D (credits for certain periods of imprisonment or detention in legal custody)`
    `regulation 9E (credits for certain spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty's forces)`
    `some other provision of the 1975 Regulations`

DECLARE `Kind of application under regulation 39` IS ONE OF
    `an application under regulation 34(1)(b)`
    `an application under regulation 35`
    `an application under regulation 36`
    `an application under regulation 37`

DECLARE `An application for a credit` HAS
    `the date the application is received` IS A DATE
    -- Regulation 39(a)(ii): the Secretary of State or the Commissioners, as the case may be, consider further time reasonable.
    `the person who decides considers it reasonable to allow further time in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Regulation 30.
DECLARE `Facts for credit while working tax credit is paid` HAS
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an employed earner in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold, who would otherwise be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the member assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earnings of each member of the couple are assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the working tax credit is paid to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lower earnings limit in force for the week` IS A NUMBER

-- Regulation 32.
DECLARE `Facts for a man approaching pensionable age` HAS
    `the person is a man` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the man's date of birth` IS A DATE
    `the date the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day` IS A DATE
    `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
    `the number of days in the year of the week that the man was absent from Great Britain` IS A NUMBER
    `the man is a self-employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the man would be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution but for profits below the small profits threshold` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the man is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lower earnings limit in force for the week` IS A NUMBER

-- Regulations 28 and 33.
DECLARE `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces` HAS
    `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
    `the earnings factors of the member for the year of the week exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the Secretary of State receives the application` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Regulation 34.
DECLARE `Facts for credit in respect of child benefit` HAS
    `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
    `child benefit is awarded to the person for any part of the week in respect of a child under the age of 12` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the partner of a person to whom child benefit is awarded for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the partner resides with the person to whom child benefit is awarded` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the partner shares responsibility for the child with that person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the partner is ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the partner is not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the partner has applied to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS A MAYBE `An application for a credit`
    -- Regulation 34(3) and (4): the earnings factors leave out any derived from credits given because of the award of child benefit.
    `the earnings factors of the person to whom child benefit is awarded for the year exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Regulation 35(6): the persons who may be credited for caring for a child under 12.
DECLARE `Relationship to the child cared for` IS ONE OF
    `a non-resident parent`
    `a grandparent`
    `a great-grandparent`
    `a great-great-grandparent`
    `a sibling, including a sibling of the half blood, a step sibling and an adopted sibling`
    `a parent's sibling, including one of the half blood, a step sibling and an adopted sibling`
    `a spouse or former spouse of a person in regulation 35(6)(a) to (f)`
    `a civil partner or former civil partner of a person in regulation 35(6)(a) to (f)`
    `a partner or former partner of a person in regulation 35(6)(a) to (h)`
    `a son or daughter of a person in regulation 35(6)(e) to (i)`
    `a spouse, former spouse, civil partner, former civil partner, partner or former partner of a parent's sibling whose son or daughter the child is`
    `none of the relationships in regulation 35(6)`

DECLARE `Facts for credit for caring for a child under 12` HAS
    `the person provided care in the week in respect of a child under the age of 12` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's relationship to the child` IS A `Relationship to the child cared for`
    `the person was ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `child benefit was awarded to another person in respect of the child, or each child, and the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that other person's earnings factors, other than those derived from a regulation 34 credit, exceed the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has applied to the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE `An application for a credit`
    `the application includes the name and date of birth of each child cared for` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State or the Commissioners requested a declaration by the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application includes a declaration by the other person that the conditions in regulation 35(2) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application specifies the week or weeks in which each child was cared for` IS A BOOLEAN
    `more than one person could be credited for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `those persons have elected, with the agreement of the other person, which of them is to be credited` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person is the one elected` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Regulation 36(2).
DECLARE `Approval as a foster parent` IS ONE OF
    `a foster parent approved under Part 5 of the Fostering Services (England) Regulations 2011`
    `a kinship carer approved under Part 5 of the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009`
    `a foster carer approved under Part 7 of the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009`
    `a foster parent approved under Part 2 of the Foster Placement (Children) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1996`
    `not approved under any of those provisions`

DECLARE `Facts for credit as a foster parent` HAS
    `the person's approval` IS A `Approval as a foster parent`
    `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has applied to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS A MAYBE `An application for a credit`

-- Regulation 37(4).
DECLARE `Relevant benefit` IS ONE OF
    `attendance allowance`
    `pension age disability payment`
    `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate`
    `an increase in the rate of disablement pension under section 104 of the 1992 Act`
    `a benefit payable as if the injury or disease were one for which disablement pension would be payable on an assessment of 100 per cent.`
    `a constant attendance allowance`
    `the daily living component of personal independence payment`
    `armed forces independence payment`
    `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate`
    `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate`
    `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate`
    `none of those benefits`

DECLARE `Facts for credit for caring` HAS
    `the hours the person cared for another person or persons in the week` IS A NUMBER
    `the benefit each person cared for is entitled to for the week` IS A LIST OF `Relevant benefit`
    `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has applied to the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE `An application for a credit`
    `the application includes a declaration by the applicant that the applicant cares for 20 or more hours in a week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application includes the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person cared for` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application says, where applicable, which relevant benefit each person cared for is entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State requested a declaration by an appropriate person as to the level of care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application includes a declaration signed by an appropriate person as to the level of care` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Regulation 38.
DECLARE `Circumstance of an additional period of credit` IS ONE OF
    `before becoming entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support`
    `after ceasing to be entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support`
    `after a week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied`

DECLARE `Facts for an additional period of credit` HAS
    `the circumstance` IS A `Circumstance of an additional period of credit`
    -- The day entitlement begins (the first circumstance), or the first day of the week in which entitlement or the satisfaction of
    -- regulation 37(2)(a) ends (the other two).
    `the day entitlement begins, or the first day of the week in which it ends` IS A DATE
    `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
    `the person is entitled in the week under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations to be credited because of carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` IS A BOOLEAN
